# Bigint division with truncation

Divides a 31-digit value and its negation by 7 to verify the quotient
truncates toward zero in both signs, producing 142857142857142857142857142857
and -142857142857142857142857142857.

>>> source
dividend: bigint = 1000000000000000000000000000000
neg_dividend: bigint = -1000000000000000000000000000000
divisor: bigint = 7

// Verifies the quotient truncates the fractional part.
truncated_quotient: bigint = dividend / divisor
print(truncated_quotient)

// Verifies truncation of a negative dividend toward zero.
neg_quotient: bigint = neg_dividend / divisor
print(neg_quotient)

<<< stdout
142857142857142857142857142857
-142857142857142857142857142857

<<< stderr
